text:
maria: Heads-up — linkbot found several outdated SDK examples in the function-calling + structured-output docs. I'm going to open a PR to modernize snippets and tighten the JSON schema examples.

sam: I'll take this. Plan: update code snippets to use `redwood.calls.invoke({tool, input})`, add a 1-line legacy shim, and add a small migration note at the top of the page.

eli: Please include an explicit envelope example that shows `\"tool\"` present and `results` marked nullable. We had a customer crash when `metadata` was missing; add an example where `metadata` is `null`.

ben: Also noticed one inline link points to `/docs/old-toolcalls` which is a 404 now. Can you run the link-checker in CI and fix redirects? The parser unit tests were failing because the sample JSON lacked the `tool` property.

sam: Drafting branch `docs/fncall-updates`. Quick snippet diff I'll include:

```js
// old
const res = await invokeTool('search', { q: 'cats' })
// new
const res = await redwood.calls.invoke({
  tool: 'search',
  input: { q: 'cats' },
})
// optional shim for legacy code
function invokeTool(name, input) {
  return redwood.calls.invoke({ tool: name, input })
}
```

sam: I'll also update the JSON schema block to show `\"tool\": \"search\"` and `\"results\": { \"type\": [\"array\",\"null\"] }`, plus a small note on parsing envelopes safely.

maria: Awesome. After you push, run the linkbot and tag me. If linkbot is clean I'll schedule a docs deploy during the maintenance window.

linkbot: Scanned /docs/function-calling and /docs/structured-output: 3 broken links found — /docs/old-toolcalls (404), /examples/old-sdk-snippet (404), /images/schema-v1.png (410). Recommend adding redirects and updating the inline examples.

eli: For the parsing example please show minimal defensive code: check for `body.results ?? []` and tolerate `metadata` being null. A one-liner in the snippet is helpful for customers.

sam: Will do. I'll add a tiny docs CI job to fail on 404s so we don't regress. PR incoming in ~20–30m. Ping here for review.

maria: Thanks — tag me on the PR and I'll add the release-note blurb.
